      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "danger, never to supplicate the wicked nor to beg of a friend",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "who has very little wealth, living nobly in adversity, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "following in the footsteps of the great,—by whom has this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "vow, as difficult ( to perform ) as walking on the edge of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "a sword, been taught to the good, ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "29. Though grown weak on account of hunger (starva-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tion ), emaciated by old age, almost unnerved and reduced",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "to a pitiable state, with all energy lost and life dying out of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "him, will the lion, foremost among those who are great in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "self-respect, ever eat withered grass when his desire is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "( habitually ) fixed solely on making a morsel of the broken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "temples of a rutting elephant ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "30 On securing even a little bone, fleshless and dirty,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "with small remnants of fat and muscles (still left), a dog is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "satisfied although it does not satisfy his hunger. (But) a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "lion kills an elephant, despising a jackal that has even fallen",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "into his clutches. Every one, though overtaken by difficulty,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "desires a fruit according to the state of his mind (or inborn",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "disposition ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "31. A dog wags his tail, falls at the feet of his master",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "( lit. feeder ); and falling on the ground exhibits his mouth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "and maw; but the lordly elephant looks grave and eats after",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "( when coaxed with ) hundreds of flattering words.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "32. In this revolving world who is not born and who is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "not dead (or, what dead person, indeed, is not born again) ?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "He ( alone is truly ) born by whose birth the family is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "raised to eminence.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "33. High-minded people have a two-fold course of action",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "like a bunch of flowers. viz. to stand at the head ( in the case",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of flowers—on the heads, ) of all men, or to wither away",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "in a forest.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
